      <tr><td valign="top"><code>SMTP_HOST</code>, <code>SMTP_USER</code>, <code>SMTP_PASS</code></td><td valign="top">For OTP email</td><td valign="top">OTP logged; not emailed.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>28.6 Demo script for a viva</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Architecture</strong> — show the folder tree and explain the SPA → proxy → Express → Mongo/GridFS path.</li>
    <li><strong>Auth</strong> — sign up, show the bcrypt hash in the database, log in, show the JWT and the profile call.</li>
    <li><strong>Content</strong> — open a note, show extracted text, TOC, progress and the read marker.</li>
    <li><strong>Assessment</strong> — start a free test, answer a few questions, submit, show the +4/−1 result and review.</li>
    <li><strong>Integrity</strong> — point out that correct answers are absent from the test payload and scoring happens on the server.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics and certificate</strong> — show the activity row, trend, and progress endpoint; explain the completion rule.</li>
    <li><strong>Admin</strong> — upload a note or create a test, then show the database record and the student view.</li>
    <li><strong>Audit</strong> — name the public admin routes and the unverified UTR flow, then describe the exact fixes.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>28.7 Final verification checklist</h3>
  <table class="compact" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="4" width="100%">
    <thead><tr><th valign="top" bgcolor="#e8f1ef">Check</th><th valign="top" bgcolor="#e8f1ef">Pass condition</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td valign="top">Backend installs and starts</td><td valign="top"><code>npm.cmd run dev</code> connects to Mongo and listens on 5000.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Frontend installs and starts</td><td valign="top">Vite serves the app; no console build errors.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Signup/login</td><td valign="top">Token persists; profile loads; invalid credentials rejected.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Password reset</td><td valign="top">OTP delivered or logged; reset token works once; old token fails.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Notes</td><td valign="top">List, read, PDF download, lazy extraction, delete.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">PYQ</td><td valign="top">Upload, filter by university/course/subject, open PDF.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Mock tests</td><td valign="top">Free and paid access, scoring, result, review, owner isolation.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Certificates</td><td valign="top">Progress correct; certificate issued once; owner-only read.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Admin</td><td valign="top">All seven sections load; uploads and purchases work.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Analytics</td><td valign="top">Trend, accuracy and history reflect real attempts.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Lint/build</td><td valign="top"><code>npm.cmd run lint</code> and <code>npm.cmd run build</code> complete.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Production serve</td><td valign="top">Express serves <code>dist</code>; deep links fall back to <code>index.html</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Secrets</td><td valign="top">No credentials in source, screenshots, logs or the guide.</td></tr>
      <tr><td valign="top">Deliverables</td><td valign="top">New HTML/PDF/DOCX/DOC present; old viva files unchanged.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>28.8 Known limitations</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Manual UPI is not verified; there is no payment webhook.</li>
    <li>Several admin read/write routes are public or only login-protected.</li>
    <li>No rate limiting, security headers or centralized validation library.</li>
    <li>No automated tests; no CI pipeline.</li>
    <li>PDF parsing is heuristic and has no draft-review step.</li>
    <li>Analytics rank/hours/average are placeholders.</li>
    <li>Activity is unbounded and duplicated across documents.</li>
    <li>Chatbot/TTS URLs hardcode localhost.</li>
    <li>Recorded lectures are static; the Course/Lecture models are underused.</li>
    <li>No notification, email verification or account deletion flow.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>28.9 Recommended next steps</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Add <code>adminOnly</code> middleware and apply it consistently.</li>
    <li>Replace the simulated payment path with verified Razorpay webhooks or admin approval.</li>
    <li>Add rate limits, upload limits, Helmet and restricted CORS.</li>
    <li>Add integration tests for auth, scoring, payment and certificate completion.</li>
    <li>Move file storage to S3-compatible object storage for scale.</li>
    <li>Introduce a real activity/leaderboard collection and scheduled aggregates.</li>
    <li>Split the admin dashboard and create a shared API client.</li>
    <li>Add content preview/edit before publishing parsed tests.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>28.10 Final summary</h3>
  <p>Mentor Lab is a full-stack learning platform built around a complete student loop: discover a course, read structured notes, attempt server-scored mock tests, review mistakes, track progress, and earn a completion certificate. It combines a React SPA with an Express/MongoDB API, GridFS file storage, JWT authentication, Razorpay integration with a demo fallback, and AI/TTS study helpers.</p>
  <p>The engineering strengths are clear separation of frontend and backend, server-side assessment integrity, ownership checks on personal records, and pragmatic use of embedded documents for quiz content. The engineering risks are equally clear: inconsistent admin authorization, unverified manual payments, and missing operational hardening. A good viva answer should present both—what works, why it was chosen, and exactly what you would change next.</p>

  
      <div style="border-left:3pt solid #0f766e; background:#f2f9f7; padding:7pt 9pt; margin:8pt 0; page-break-inside:avoid;">
        <p style="font-size:8pt; font-weight:bold; letter-spacing:1pt; color:#0f766e; margin:0 0 2pt 0;">Closing note</p>
        <div>
    
    <p>Know the request path, know the data model, know the scoring formula, and know the three security fixes. Those four things cover most of the project’s technical story.</p>
  </div>
